            "needId": "detail:3",
            "type": "detail",
            "heading": "Market Demand and Skill Match Come First",
            "kind": "items",
            "items": [
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Market demand / future-proofing"
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "A career can look exciting, well-paid, and secure everywhere online and still have almost no real market for your specific combination of skill and location."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Being able to admire a role and being able to become genuinely good at its daily work are two different tests."
              }
            ],
            "sourceSectionId": "floor",
            "sourceNeedIndex": 3
          },
          {
            "needId": "detail:6",
            "type": "detail",
            "heading": "Some Factors Carry More Weight Than Others",
            "kind": "items",
            "items": [
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "The tier order above is not arbitrary."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Hygiene factors like pay, job security, and working conditions can create real dissatisfaction when they are missing, but adding more of them stops improving satisfaction fast once a baseline is covered."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "This is the research reason pay sits in The Shape tier instead of at the very top."
              }
            ],
            "sourceSectionId": "why-order",
            "sourceNeedIndex": 6
          }
        ]
      },
      "type": "summary",
      "title": "\"Chase the Highest Pay\" Both Fail"
